<title>USA: NS Group Inc cuts Q4 Sept 28 loss.</title>
<headline>NS Group Inc cuts Q4 Sept 28 loss.</headline>
<dateline>NEWPORT, Ky. 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>(in thousands, except per share amounts)</p>
<p>			   Three Months Ended  Fiscal Year Ended(1)</p>
<p>			    Sep 28,    Sep 30,   Sep 28,    Sep 30,</p>
<p>				 1996	1995	 1996	1995</p>
<p> Net sales	     $111,595   $ 86,004  $409,382   $371,352</p>
<p>Loss before</p>
<p>  extraordinary item  (3,874)    (6,107)  (10,457)    (5,056)</p>
<p>Extraordinary item,</p>
<p>  net of taxes		  -    (5,200)	   -    (5,200)</p>
<p> Net loss		 (3,874)   (11,307)  (10,457)   (10,256)</p>
<p>Per common share:</p>
<p>Loss before</p>
<p>   extraordinary item   (.28)	(.44)     (.76)	(.36)</p>
<p>  Extraordinary item	  -	(.38)	   -	(.38)</p>
<p>  Net loss		  (.28)	(.82)     (.76)	(.74)</p>
<p>Weighted average</p>
<p>shares</p>
<p>  outstanding	    13,809     13,809    13,809     13,809</p>
<p> EBITDA (2)		 9,867	  812    32,594     31,141</p>
<p>NOTE:  1996 Q4 includes a $1.0 million gain from settlement of warrantee claims and a $2.7 million charge from certain revisions to estimates of annual tax benefits.</p>
<p>(1) The Company's fiscal year ends on the last Saturday of September.  The first quarter and fiscal year periods of fiscal 1996 and 1995 were 13 and 14 week and 52 and 53 week periods, respectively.</p>
<p>(2) Represents earnings before interest, taxes, depreciation and amortization, and is calculated as income before extraordinary items plus interest expense, taxes, depreciation and amortization.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
